            <ArticleTitle>[Proglumetacin in acute periodontitis. Effectiveness and tolerance].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>66-71</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The Authors show the results of a clinical trial carried out on two groups of patients affected by acute periodontitis. Patients were treated with proglumetacin or ketoprofen, respectively; the efficacy and tolerability of these two drugs were analyzed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
